## What to deliver

Build and rig the bastion up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a massive masonry keep base, a collector crown
ringing the summit, a gate in the front wall, and a beacon atop the spire. The
required interface is the three auto **`crown_spin`**, **`gate_raise`**, and
**`beacon_spin`** joints — each driven by a decorative auto-play animation you
author as F-curves — that turn the crown, lift the gate up and down, and turn the
beacon on their own, while the `base` stays fixed. Produce **every** required part,
joint, and animation; you may add your own extra parts, joints, or auto-play
animations on top, but do not drop or contradict the required interface. When you
are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
